Lesson 1: Computer Networks and the Internet
Beginner level · Chapter 1 · Study time: approximately 25 minutes
Part 1 — What is a computer network?
A computer network is a group of devices connected so they can communicate and share information or resources.

Examples include:
- Your laptop connecting to your home Wi-Fi.
- Your phone sending a WhatsApp message.
- A college computer accessing an online assignment.
- A bank server communicating with an ATM.







